# Non-secret EKVM_* knobs for local dev. Nothing loads this file automatically: export via
# your shell or direnv (a copied `.env` is gitignored). The config contract is layered,
# flags > env (`EKVM_*`) > file (`.ekvm.toml`) > defaults (see `AGENTS.md`); all of
# these layers are wired today, and this file documents the env one.
# Env is the ephemeral layer: per-shell overrides, CI, and containers (where you inject env, not
# files), and it is what `cargo run -p ekvm-cli` inherits. For anything persistent (a self-hoster's
# artifact paths, house defaults, operator ceilings) prefer `.ekvm.toml`: it is discovered
# by walking up from the cwd like `.gitignore`, and `cargo xtask self-host` writes a starter one. The
# Configuration and Operator policy sections of `docs/cli.md` document that layer in full, including
# the operator-policy knobs env cannot set.
# ekvm holds NO secrets: the engine needs no API key, and tenancy/auth belong to the hoster.
# If you find yourself adding a credential here, the change is mis-scoped.

# --- Logging ---
# EKVM_LOG=warn                      # error | warn | info | debug | trace (stderr; stdout is the run result)

# --- Boot & exec ---
# EKVM_FIRECRACKER=firecracker       # the firecracker binary: a PATH name or an absolute path
# EKVM_KERNEL=artifacts/vmlinux      # uncompressed ELF/PVH guest kernel (`cargo xtask fetch-artifacts`)
# Default rootfs: boots to a console prompt but has no in-guest agent (the `run --demo-boot` path).
# EKVM_ROOTFS=artifacts/rootfs.ext4  # base rootfs; a read-write boot runs against a fresh per-VM copy
# EKVM_MARKER=login:                 # console substring meaning "the guest reached userspace"
#                                     # (tied to this image; change it if you swap the rootfs)
# To run code in the guest, point at the built guest rootfs (`cargo xtask build-rootfs`) and its
# readiness marker (the two go together: the marker is the line the agent prints once it's listening):
# EKVM_ROOTFS=artifacts/rootfs-guest.ext4
# EKVM_MARKER=GUEST-READY
#   e.g.  EKVM_ROOTFS=artifacts/rootfs-guest.ext4 EKVM_MARKER=GUEST-READY \
#           cargo run -p ekvm-cli -- run -- python3 -c 'print(2 + 2)'
# Not env knobs, set in code deliberately (docs/architecture.md): the read-only base +
# per-run tmpfs overlay, bulk read-only input via a second block device, and bulk writable output via
# a third (pulled back with `RunningVm::collect_outputs`). Don't hunt for an
# `EKVM_READONLY`/`EKVM_INPUT`/`EKVM_OUTPUT`; they're per-VM boot inputs the caller sets, not
# layered config.
